---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us — Our Mission & Editorial Policy"
  description="Learn about InfluenzaSymptoms.com — our mission to provide evidence-based, medically reviewed information about influenza symptoms. Editorial policy and medical review process."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 prose">
    <h1>About InfluenzaSymptoms.com</h1>

    <div class="callout-info">
      <strong>Our Mission:</strong> To provide clear, accurate, and evidence-based information about influenza symptoms — empowering people to understand their health and know when to seek care.
    </div>

    <h2>Why We Built This</h2>
    <p>
      When you or a loved one has flu symptoms, you want answers — fast. But searching online often leads to
      overwhelming, ad-cluttered pages from general health portals that bury the information you need.
    </p>
    <p>
      InfluenzaSymptoms.com is different. We focus exclusively on influenza symptoms — providing
      detailed, organized, and accessible information that helps you understand what's happening
      and what to do about it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="editorial-policy">Editorial Policy</h2>
    <h3>Our Content Standards</h3>
    <p>Every article on this site follows strict editorial guidelines:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Evidence-based:</strong> All health claims are supported by peer-reviewed research or authoritative health organizations (CDC, WHO, NHS)</li>
      <li><strong>Sourced:</strong> We cite our sources with direct links so you can verify information yourself</li>
      <li><strong>Current:</strong> Content is regularly reviewed and updated. Every page shows its last review date</li>
      <li><strong>Transparent:</strong> We clearly distinguish between established medical facts and emerging research</li>
      <li><strong>Accessible:</strong> Written in clear, plain language with medical terms explained</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What We Don't Do</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>We do <strong>not</strong> provide personal medical advice or diagnoses</li>
      <li>We do <strong>not</strong> recommend specific treatments for individual cases</li>
      <li>We do <strong>not</strong> replace the relationship between you and your healthcare provider</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="medical-review">Medical Review Process</h2>
    <p>
      Our content is researched and written by health communicators with experience in medical writing.
      All articles undergo review for medical accuracy, clarity, and alignment with current clinical guidelines.
    </p>
    <p>
      We prioritize information from:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)</li>
      <li>World Health Organization (WHO)</li>
      <li>National Health Service (NHS UK)</li>
      <li>Peer-reviewed medical journals</li>
      <li>Clinical practice guidelines from recognized medical organizations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our Commitment to You</h2>
    <p>
      Health information affects real decisions and real lives. We take that responsibility seriously.
      If you ever find information on this site that you believe is inaccurate or outdated, please
      contact us so we can review and correct it.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
